<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n93981" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σίγλος</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σίκλος</span></b>  (the latter form in <i><span class="en">
			LXX
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			J.
		</span></i>, and <i><span class="en">
			S.
		</span></i> (v. infr.)), ὁ,= Hebr. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>shekel</i>, a weight (<i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>Ex.</u>
				30.23
			</span></i>, al.) or coin (ib.<i><span class="en">
				<u>Le.</u>
				5.15
			</span></i>); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δραχμὴ μία τὸ ἥμισυ τοῦ
			ς</span>. ib.<i><span class="en">
				<u>Ex.</u>
				39.2
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				38.26
			</span></i>); but 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ ς . . . Ἀττικὰς δέχεται δραχμὰς
					τέτταρας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					J.
					<u>AJ</u>
					3.8.2
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>
			
				s.v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σίκλος</span>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> the Persian
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ς</span>. was the <i><span class="en">
				1
			</span></i>/<i><span class="en">
				3000t
			</span></i>h part of the Baby lonian silver talent, half the silver
			stater of Asia Minor, and =
			<i><span class="en">
				7
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				1
			</span></i>/<i><span class="en">
				2
			</span></i>
			
				Att.
			
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀβολοί</span>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>An.</u>
				1.5.6
			</span></i>; or <i><span class="en">
				8
			</span></i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀβολοί</span>, acc. to <i><span class="en">
				Phot.
			</span></i>, quoting <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				1094
			</span></i> (perh. erroneously, instead of for sense <i><span class="en">
				11
			</span></i>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>ear-ring</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Phot.
			</span></i>, cf. sq. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b> in
				<i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				34.8.7
			</span></i>, prob. corrupt for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Σικελικός</span>.</div>
